## Cloudflare DNS

This box may have a zone-scoped Cloudflare DNS API token at `/home/{{USERNAME}}/.cloudflare/token`.

- Use it only for the Cloudflare zone configured for this Dev Boxer host.
- Cloudflare zone: `{{CF_ZONE_NAME}}`
- It is intended for creating and updating DNS records for project subdomains.
- Do not print, commit, or transmit the token.
- When exposing a local web project, create a proxied CNAME to the existing Cloudflare Tunnel target and add a matching cloudflared ingress rule for the local port. Prefix the subdomain with `public-` only when the user explicitly wants it openly reachable; otherwise the `*.{{CF_ZONE_NAME}}` Access wildcard will gate it behind login.
- Before relying on Access for a new subdomain, verify it actually challenges: `curl -I https://<host>/` should redirect to `cloudflareaccess.com/cdn-cgi/access/login`. If it returns 200 directly, the wildcard app isn't in place — flag it to the user before continuing.
- If the token file is missing, ask the user whether DNS is manual before trying to create records.

